package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The exporter uses unique private temporary files and atomic replacement, preserves complete invoice data and the sentinel under concurrency and the seeded symlink attack, preserves an existing destination on failure, and cleans temporary artifacts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart baseline, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, SSH, data, and export behavior.","limitations":["Signal and every possible early-exit path were not dynamically injected; cleanup on those paths is supported primarily by inspection of the installed traps, alongside direct success and rename-failure tests.","No independent lifecycle snapshot inventories the task directory itself; final task state is established by executor commands, while lifecycle evidence independently confirms platform, boot, service, listener, temporary-file, and package health."]}
